{
  "case_id": "2022-21-476",
  "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Can I give you a hypothetical? It's not really a hypothetical, because I happen to have two clerks in my chambers this year who are engaged, so, in looking at this case and preparing this case, I looked at their websites."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Where?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, what do we -- what do we do --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- that they\nshould be married. What's the difference\nbetween that and I don't believe black people\nand white people should get married?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Waggoner",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the First Amendment is broad\nenough to cover the lesbian website designer and\nthe Catholic calligrapher. The line is that no\none on any side of any debate has to be\ncompelled to express a message that violates\ntheir core convictions because, as this Court\nfound, it's demeaning to them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: -- can I ask you a\nhypothetical that just sort of helps me to flesh\nthat out?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: It may be an edge case\nmeaning it could fall on either side, you're not\nsure?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: If your -- if\nyour client's website was the same as it is, but\nthe only indication of any limitation was a tag\nline at the end saying these services are for\nheterosexual couples only, could that\nconstitutionally be applied under the Colorado\nstatute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Twenty states",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0001-0009",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. WAGGONER: Twenty states filed an\namicus brief in support of Ms. Smith\nand expressed to this Court that they're\napplying their public accommodation law to\nprovide message-based object -- protections,\njust like the Court did in Hurley, following the\nsame test that's being articulated today, and\nthey've been doing it successfully."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Waggoner",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. WAGGONER: Because they're\ncreating speech. In those other examples,\nspeech is not at issue, that is creating speech,\nannouncing a wedding, or announcing anything."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: So, for you, as -- as there's a effort to protect both the equal rights of gay and lesbian people and same-sex couples at the same time protect free speech rights, your line is look at whether the action of the business involves speech?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. OLSON: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The central dispute here is what public accommodations law target when they require a business to provide equal access to its services. The company claims that because it wants to sell websites, the law somehow targets expression and therefore violates the First Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: I understand that. I understand -- the complicating factor here -- fact here is this is not a hotel, this is not a restaurant, this is not a riverboat or a train. I'm interested in the intersection of public accommodations law and speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. OLSON: So I think that the historical record is sparse on both sides, but the two things I would say, Justice Thomas, is what we don't see is a history of public accommodation laws carving out speech. They all are laws of general applicability that apply to all those operating a trade to the public. They don't say except those engaged in expressive conduct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And what this company seeks, if you look at the -- the specific prayer for relief in the complaint, is a total permission to turn away every same-sex couple, even if they seek exactly the same website that an opposite-sex couple that they will provide."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let me see if I understand your argument. I understand you to be arguing that a website designer can put anything it wants on a standardized website, even if that includes a denunciation of same-sex marriage. Is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "sole basis that the company seeks relief from this Court is they would like an injunction that says so long as -- if -- if this is going to be used for a same-sex wedding, then we need not provide it. And -- and so it's a status-based discrimination that they seek from this Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that website designer is not going to be serving a same-sex couple if the website designer puts that on the website. They're turning away same-sex couples by doing that, are they not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does -- does every press release writer, freelance writer have to write a press release for the Church of Scientology, say, even though the beliefs of that institution may be inimical to that person?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the answer is yes, Colorado would compel that person?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 92,
        "start": 92
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What's different about this case? Because -- I'll just finish the question. I -- I know you're already ready to answer it. But we have an individual who says she will sell and does sell to everyone all manner of websites. But she won't sell a website that requires her to express a view about marriage that she finds offensive to her religious beliefs. What's the difference between the two cases? I'm struggling to understand."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 93,
        "start": 93
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I still -- I'm -- I'm looking for the distinction between the two cases. One you say is okay and the other one not okay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0004-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You can't change their religious belief, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0004-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And you protect religious beliefs under the statute, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0004-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Phillips did go through a re-education training program pursuant to Colorado law, did he not, Mr. Olson?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0004-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It was a re-education program, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0004-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 96,
        "start": 96
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If it were a public accommodation, it would still have a First Amendment right, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice JACKSON",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0004-0015",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 106,
        "start": 106
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Am I right about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0005-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 110,
        "start": 110
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF BRIAN H. FLETCHER FOR THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE RESPONDENTS MR. FLETCHER: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: My friend, Ms. Waggoner, offered a two-part test this morning for when a commercial business is entitled to an exemption from a generally applicable public accommodations law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0005-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 110,
        "start": 110
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that, Your Honor. First is I think both Spence and Hurley itself talked about the importance of how an onlooker would look at the message and -- and who the onlooker would attribute the message to. So I think you certainly could -- could -- could build on that. And, again, here, there's no evidence whatsoever that -- that anyone would look at a wedding website designed by 303 Creative and say, oh, that is, you know, the -- the speech and beliefs of the designer as opposed to the couple getting married."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0005-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 112,
        "start": 112
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I do think the Court in -- in Rumsfeld was dealing with the sort of compulsion that is significantly different from the compulsion here. In what other case have we upheld compelling speech, in other words, not simply just restricting speech but actually compelling an individual to engage in speech contrary to her beliefs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0006-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 131,
        "start": 131
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I --I ask this because a lot of the arguments on your side seemed to view public accommodations -- that if it's a public accommodations law, it's generally okay, there's no problem with it. And that's why I want to know how far that can be expanded."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Mr. Fletcher)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0006-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 131,
        "start": 131
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Some selectivity wouldn't take them out, but I think the farther the state wanders from the sort of traditional core of commercial establishments that hold themselves out as serving the public, the weaker the state interest is."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Mr. Fletcher)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0006-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 139,
        "start": 139
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My favorite one is this Court's decision in Runyon versus McCrary, which was about a school that wanted to exclude children of particular races, and it said the reason we want to do this is because segregation is important to our beliefs and that's what we want to teach. And this Court said, you are free to teach segregation in your school, but you can't act on that belief by excluding children of particular races."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fcc45048ea693ddfe5dfb21d388f9e04d11af7c5ed697b4eba372307713cfbac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fcc45048ea69-0006-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 139,
        "start": 139
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Last question. You said to Justice Jackson that you didn't want to belabor the point, but her hypothetical is exactly the kind of hypothetical that you're concerned about."
    },
